{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1206663-db-charm-commentary-part-1","id":1206663,"title":"DB Charm Commentary (part 1)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-13T14:30:53-07:00","id":1206663,"title":"DB Charm Commentary (part 1)","content":"I've done some rules analyses for parts of the Solar charmset before (especially crafting and persona charms), so I figured I'd make some comments on the current draft of the Dragon-Blooded rules. This is especially intended for folks who are on the fence on the kickstarter, but there are a handful of comments in here that I hope make it to the devs as well.<br /> <br /> <b>General Rules:</b><ul><li>DBs still have a major advantage in backgrounds, but only a minor one in skills compared to the 10 extra dots they had in previous editions. The fact that DB characters are created at Essence 2 rather than 1 (having trained it up through schooling and rigorous training) helps balance &quot;starting&quot; DBs against starting Solars.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Anima effects:</b><ul><li>You can sense direction and rough distance to someone in your sworn kinship. That's awesome. That's a major plot driver.</li> <li>Anima flux is a murder machine. Someone caught in close combat with three fire-aspects had better not get crashed. Even if they normally have Hardness, it's set to zero during crash, and they'll take 9 dice of lethal every turn.</li> <li>Air is great for falling, but loses out in combat effectiveness. People attacking an Air-aspect from range lose half a success on average, at a cost of 3 motes per attack. Meanwhile, for 0 motes, 40% of the people attacking an Earth-aspect fly backwards or fall down every turn. As a reminder, knockback damage in this game is brutal: 3 levels of bashing plus another 5 dice of bashing for this one-range-band throw. That's an average of 2 levels of bashing damage per turn to each close attacker, plus eating up some of their movement actions.</li> <li>Water-aspects can survive underwater long-term now! Very nice.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Charms:</b><ul><li>There's no equivalent to Supernal (unless I missed something). You're limited by your Essence on charms, full stop. However...</li> <li>Signature charms are all Essence 3! That's awesome! I had expected them higher.</li> <li>There seem to be no more teamwork charms outside of Integrity. I'm expecting some of them make it into War, but there aren't any so far that allow Dragon-blooded to combine their efforts on a single action.</li> <li>Dragon-blooded have no equivalent to Monkey Leap Technique. They can <i>fly</i> more easily (and Brawl has the wonderful Flying Whirlwind Razor) but if a particular DB can't fly, they can't effectively follow a Solar who's invested even a little in Dodge and Athletics.</li> <li>The expansion of the charm trees is really great to see. The classics are still here, and I've got a bunch of NPCs whose capabilities are still well-represented here, but there's plenty of room for new NPCs who use the same abilities in different ways.</li> <li>Dragon-blooded can't grapple Legendary-sized creatures. Bummer. I might need to make a custom charm for that.</li> <li>Humble Exemplar Attitude and Graven Stone Edict are fantastic. Dragon-blooded Bureaucracy is pretty damn sweet overall.</li> <li>There's a fair amount of &quot;reroll non-1 failures&quot;, which nicely lets some charms continue to take advantage of those 1s. I'm expecting to see a bunch of those for Abyssals some day.</li> <li>Dragon-blooded Craft has no charms above Essence 3.</li> <li>Safety Among Enemies is still great.</li> <li>Frozen Heart Prana = &quot;I Don't Care How Hot You Are Stance&quot;</li> <li>Shadow-Immolating Talon reinforces the false idea that torture obtains correct information. Sigh.</li> <li>The rest of the Investigation tree is fantastic. It's not as flat-out powerful as it used to be, but it's incredibly useful, and Dragon-blooded are going to be able to track down Solars on a regular basis.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>General Notes:</b><ul><li>The elemental flavor in these charms is fantastic.</li> <li>I wasn't sure how I would like having charms from one element in an ability that's mostly about another element. It works well. It'll be a little weird for long-time players, but once you accept the idea of every DB having some of every element in them, it works just fine.</li> <li>The Solar archetype of &quot;I craft to solve every problem&quot; does not exist for the Dragon-Blooded. There's no charm that speeds artifact creation, and no way to reasonably attempt Artifact 5 or N/A crafting with any expectation of success.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Are There Still Tiers of Power?</b><br /> Yes. Dragon-blooded charms are definitively weaker than Solar charms. The power gap seems to be smaller than it was in 2e or even 1e, but it's still there. When the charms have similar effects, nearly every Solar charm is flat-out twice as good...<br /> <br /> ...with the exception of the Signature charms. Signature charms are Solar-level, and they're basically all great.<br /> <br /> DB excellencies do more than just adding dice, which is nice, but rerolling 6s isn't as good when your dice pool is smaller. Plus DBs have to buy excellencies instead of getting them for free.<br /> <br /> I don't think anyone really expected or wanted Dragon-Blooded to be on par with Solars of the same experience and focus anyway, so I find this to be just fine. I just wanted to address it since it's such a common question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Current project: <a href=\"https://monsterambulance.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Monster Ambulance</a>, wherein you save monsters. In your ambulance.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2240-colin_fredericks","name":"Colin_Fredericks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2240_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T14:53:21-07:00","id":1206670,"title":"","content":"Yeah, my only concerns right now are<br /> <br /> a) the power gap in Anima effects with Air on the low end and Earth at the top (though Water is sort of perpendicularly amazing in a non-mechanically measurable way)<br /> <br /> b) it seems difficult to maintain Air or Wood Aura in combat since other than the Dodge and Brawl (and we can go ahead and assume Melee) excellencies, they don\u2019t have a lot of usable defensive Charms. Could really use some Air dodge-monkey effects, but we\u2019ll see if Air Dragon Style lets you Aang-around your opponents.<br /> <br /> There has also been some raised concernes about xp scaling (which Vance said he\u2019ll take another look at). But i\u2019m less concerned there because that\u2019s a lot easier to customize to taste at individual tables. My solution is just going to be to give Essence 2 characters access to ONE signature charm of their choice early to represent being prodigies, and let the players have access to their choice of the cool toys early while still leaving them more broadly gated off for setting-balance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T15:20:11-07:00","id":1206680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colin_Fredericks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1206663-db-charm-commentary-part-1#post1206663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Air is great for falling, but loses out in combat effectiveness. People attacking an Air-aspect from range lose half a success on average, at a cost of 3 motes per attack. Meanwhile, for 0 motes, 40% of the people attacking an Earth-aspect fly backwards or fall down every turn. As a reminder, knockback damage in this game is brutal: 3 levels of bashing plus another 5 dice of bashing for this one-range-band throw. That's an average of 2 levels of bashing damage per turn to each close attacker, plus eating up some of their movement actions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The ability to spend 3 times as many motes to penalize someone as they have to if they want to cancel out that penalty is indeed hot garbage, but I think you're underestimating the impact of free vertical movement and being able to ignore difficult terrain.<br /> <br /> Also, unless the specific rules of Heaven Thunder Hammer apply to every instance of knockback (there is no indication of such in the rules text), flinging somebody away does not, by default, result in damage. Maybe if you find a way to knock them upwards. But the idea that the dominant strategy in Dragon-Blooded personal combat is for participants to try and get under each other so they can catapult their opponent into the air seems profoundly silly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colin_Fredericks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1206663-db-charm-commentary-part-1#post1206663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]Shadow-Immolating Talon reinforces the false idea that torture obtains correct information. Sigh.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That seems like an incredibly bad faith reading of the ability in question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T16:00:35-07:00","id":1206702,"title":"","content":"All Dragon-Blooded Abilities actually have one more Essence 5 Charm than they seem to.<br /> <br /> Because at Essence 5, a Dragon-Blood can buy a second Signature Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T19:03:13-07:00","id":1206757,"title":"","content":"I think it is possible for a Terrestrial Exalt to craft artifact 5 with decent reliability, if they use Imago-Hatching Realization (either waiting multiple stories or spending wxp to reset) on every roll, and also are essence 5 using every charm, including the repurchase and either of Eternal Omphalos Forge and Blazing Dragon-Smith Arete. And have 5 attribute+5 ability+speciality. And get at least a 1-point stunt. Spending willpower wouldn't be amiss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T20:54:28-07:00","id":1206782,"title":"","content":"On teamwork, don't overlook the Distract-boosting Charms. Life-Swelling Sap Strike in Archery buffs a Distract the archer uses, and Become the Wave and Swift-Striking Tide in Brawl both allow the brawler to get more benefit out of being the beneficiary of a Distract action. If that trend continues through the rest of our combat abilities, that suggests we'll have some fun options for &quot;set 'em up and knock 'em down&quot; combos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21733-ascension","name":"Ascension","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21733_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T01:19:23-07:00","id":1206817,"title":"","content":"Shadow-Immolating Talon reinforces the idea that torture has to be <i>backed up by magic</i> to obtain correct information.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T01:54:55-07:00","id":1206827,"title":"","content":"If our standard for torture is &quot;attacking a person who is engaged with you in mortal combat&quot;, then pretty much every Exalted character ever is a torturer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T02:16:42-07:00","id":1206829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1206663-db-charm-commentary-part-1?p=1206680#post1206680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, unless the specific rules of Heaven Thunder Hammer apply to every instance of knockback (there is no indication of such in the rules text), flinging somebody away does not, by default, result in damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going to say that. There are lots of effects that knock people back, but only Heaven Thunder Hammer and one of the DB charms (I forget which) say they inflict falling damage. So I'm pretty sure the Earth anima just knocks you prone or back.<br /> <br /> Which is good, but it's not throwing damage onto people (besides the 1 from the anima damage).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T02:19:29-07:00","id":1206830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1206663-db-charm-commentary-part-1?p=1206670#post1206670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Y]It seems difficult to maintain Air or Wood Aura in combat since other than the Dodge and Brawl (and we can go ahead and assume Melee) excellencies, they don\u2019t have a lot of usable defensive Charms. Could really use some Air dodge-monkey effects, but we\u2019ll see if Air Dragon Style lets you Aang-around your opponents.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are some Air-aspected dodge charms. Not as many as fire, but some.<br /> <br /> (And also a couple of Water ones, which other than the sig seem to be about disengaging. Which seems appropriate.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T07:44:31-07:00","id":1206878,"title":"","content":"I'm not saying the devs <i>set out</i> to design a pro-torture charm, just that they <i>did</i> design one. If y'all want to jump to the charm's defense, I don't need to respond to you.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3443_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3443\" data-vbnamecard=\"3443\">aluminiumtrioxid</a> The movement is a good point. I'm so used to literally every Solar in my party having Monkey Leap Technique that I completely overlooked that, but yes, definitely handy.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a> Interesting points on maintaining aura. I was going to suggest the defensive Archery charms, but now that I look at it they're all Essence 3+ (as are the Air dodge charms). Maybe there will be more Wood in Resistance? If Thrown doesn't pick up some defensive charms, air aura is definitely going to be hard to maintain.<br /> <br /> As for knockback damage, I'd just like it to be explicit. I already have to extrapolate charm effects to make Flawless Handiwork Method useful. (Rules-as-written it charges you 6 motes to erase all your 10s.) Don't make me wonder whether I should be extrapolating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Current project: <a href=\"https://monsterambulance.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Monster Ambulance</a>, wherein you save monsters. In your ambulance.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2240-colin_fredericks","name":"Colin_Fredericks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2240_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T08:42:57-07:00","id":1206898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colin_Fredericks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1206663-db-charm-commentary-part-1?p=1206878#post1206878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for knockback damage, I'd just like it to be explicit. I already have to extrapolate charm effects to make Flawless Handiwork Method useful. (Rules-as-written it charges you 6 motes to erase all your 10s.) Don't make me wonder whether I should be extrapolating.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right but it is explicit, there is no reason to think that getting moved a range band causes falling damage. Heaven thunder hammer both moves a character and is called out as inflicting falling damage explicitly. This is the same for Firmament shattering impact which explicitly calls out when falling damage is applied.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T08:56:54-07:00","id":1206903,"title":"","content":"I don't think they really need specify stuff as <i>blindingly </i><i>obvious </i>as &quot;if you pay motes to reroll successful dice you keep the successes&quot;.<br /> <br /> They're not writing a computer program. It's a rule book for humans to read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 04-14-2018, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T09:32:02-07:00","id":1206914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1206663-db-charm-commentary-part-1?p=1206898#post1206898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right but it is explicit, there is no reason to think that getting moved a range band causes falling damage. Heaven thunder hammer both moves a character and is called out as inflicting falling damage explicitly. This is the same for Firmament shattering impact which explicitly calls out when falling damage is applied.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Unless your moved a range band up, and then fall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T09:47:19-07:00","id":1206922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dragon-blooded can't grapple Legendary-sized creatures. Bummer. I might need to make a custom charm for that. </div> </div> </div>That doesn\u2019t strike me as something DBs should be able to do (sans warstrider anyway). They need to use clever coordination and command forces, etc, taking on a behemoth. Wrestling a behemoth one on one is very Solar flavored to me (even a Lunar i\u2019d assume would shift to compreable size to be able to do it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T11:34:25-07:00","id":1206966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colin_Fredericks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1206663-db-charm-commentary-part-1?p=1206878#post1206878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying the devs <i>set out</i> to design a pro-torture charm, just that they <i>did</i> design one. If y'all want to jump to the charm's defense, I don't need to respond to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.. isn't really helping the case that you're giving the Charm a fair shake.<br /> <br /> Can you unpack this for us at least?<br /> <br /> You don't want to talk to people defending the Charm... OK. But I think for the sake of good discussion, you should at least explain your claim to those of us confused by it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1206663-db-charm-commentary-part-1?p=1206922#post1206922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That doesn\u2019t strike me as something DBs should be able to do (sans warstrider anyway). They need to use clever coordination and command forces, etc, taking on a behemoth. Wrestling a behemoth one on one is very Solar flavored to me (even a Lunar i\u2019d assume would shift to compreable size to be able to do it).</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded. Dragonbloods don't really seem like they should be grappling behemoths. They should be grabbing Grand artifact weapons specifically designed for fighting such creatures, and then use good tactics to take it down.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T17:39:36-07:00","id":1207079,"title":"","content":"Solar Exalted seem to have more Charms that hit (or can hit) single targets multiple times, whereas Dragon-Blooded seem to have more Charms that must hit multiple targets.<br /> <br /> Hammer on Iron Technique versus Fist-Spinning Maelstrom. Also, Hanging Tree Technique.<br /> <br /> Solar Brawl's Falling Hammer Strike allows a single Solar to keep stacking onslaught penalties on a target, as well as to preserve the penalties of Ox-Stunning Blow, and Ferocious Jab exploits onslaught penalty for greater damage.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Dragon-Blooded Brawl's Hammering Wave Technique is nowhere near as reliable as Falling Hammer Strike (though it at least boosts damage), so the Dragon-Blood needs to rely more on allies to impose onslaught penalties before she attacks. Pleasantly, Pounding Surf Style and Hammer Wave Technique lead upwards into other team-oriented Charms like Become the Wave and Swift-Striking Tide.<br /> <br /> <br /> The design intent seems to be making Dragon-Blooded effective team-players against single opponents, for players fighting a boss character, while also making high-level Dragon-Blooded effective boss characters against teams of player characters.<br /> <br /> Solar Exalted, on the other hand, have no particular weakness when working in a team, but their Charms are generally built to allow them to fight alone and win, as long as they are allowed to fight in their specialty. There's no particular emphasis about fighting single opponents or greater numbers, either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T17:42:23-07:00","id":1207081,"title":"","content":"Dragonblooded craft stood out to me the most, mainly in how limited it is. Like I have no issues with Dragonblooded have problems making Art 5's and unlikely to make Art N/A's, but I feel that at ESS 3 it being a crapshoot to make Artifact 3's? Ironically this is where 2e craft was better, as there you were discouraged from making something like Art 5 as a DB unless you wanted to spend a long time. It'd be like a magnum opus for your character but shit you could do it as terminus wasn't a thing. Here you're forced to hit a goal number before a certain number of rolls where not only start over again, but the artifact you wanted to make is <i>gone forever</i>.<br /> <br /> I really feel this shouldn't be the case. Maybe I'm wrong and there will be some answers later in the book. Do the other abilities have some way to increase dice pools? Will there be an artifact that really helps DB crafting? (I hope not, as this'd feel mandatory to take). I'm going to wait until Tuesday until I decide to start reeving up that homebrew chainsaw.<br /> <br /> I also hope the &quot;Get these charms if you want to stand a prayer at making Art 4&quot; charms are not in Heirs. If anything that'd feel like DLC practices where you cut up a whole game and then sell parts of it off in DLC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":1183,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","user":"Sandact6","date":". 04-14-2018, 08:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T19:17:00-07:00","id":1207116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1206663-db-charm-commentary-part-1?p=1207081#post1207081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragonblooded craft stood out to me the most, mainly in how limited it is. Like I have no issues with Dragonblooded have problems making Art 5's and unlikely to make Art N/A's, but I feel that at ESS 3 it being a crapshoot to make Artifact 3's? Ironically this is where 2e craft was better, as there you were discouraged from making something like Art 5 as a DB unless you wanted to spend a long time. It'd be like a magnum opus for your character but shit you could do it as terminus wasn't a thing. Here you're forced to hit a goal number before a certain number of rolls where not only start over again, but the artifact you wanted to make is <i>gone forever</i>.<br /> <br /> I really feel this shouldn't be the case. Maybe I'm wrong and there will be some answers later in the book. Do the other abilities have some way to increase dice pools? Will there be an artifact that really helps DB crafting? (I hope not, as this'd feel mandatory to take). I'm going to wait until Tuesday until I decide to start reeving up that homebrew chainsaw.<br /> <br /> I also hope the &quot;Get these charms if you want to stand a prayer at making Art 4&quot; charms are not in Heirs. If anything that'd feel like DLC practices where you cut up a whole game and then sell parts of it off in DLC.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're underestimating dragon blooded craft. Using everything available at ESS 2, and 1-point stunts., a dragon blood can average 13.6 successes per roll (19 dice with double 9s, rerolling 2 non-1 failures, 1 success from willpower). At terminus 6, that averages 57.6 successes. Which is enough for artifact 3 &gt;50% of the time. With higher essence and/or the right signatures, the odds get very good.<br /> At ESS 3, you can make artifact 4 with variable rates of success depending on which signature you use but you can get over 50%.<br /> Getting artifact 5 with &gt;50% success rate doesn't require anything not currently previewed (it does require essence 5, carefully chosen signatures, and a large investment of motes, willpower and craft XP, but not theoretical out-of-ability or out-of-book charms)<br /> Artifact NA is probably beyond someone with just the previewed charms, but I don't think that's a flaw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T20:52:30-07:00","id":1207145,"title":"","content":"Yea I only saw your forum post after I posted my message. It did make me rethink my mind about the topic, but now I wonder if the Wood craft sig charm is a One True Build issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T03:13:48-07:00","id":1207207,"title":"","content":"Compared to the Fire charm that gives you Essence non-charm successes on every craft roll in the project, I can't really see Wood as the One True Build.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T03:47:20-07:00","id":1207212,"title":"","content":"I was personally impressed by the Earth charm increasing the project terminus by half your essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T05:39:38-07:00","id":1207225,"title":"","content":"I think there's a trade-off between potential for high-rated artifacts and cheapness of low-rated artifacts.<br /> Imago-Hatching Realization costs 10 motes, 1 wp, and 5 gxp per use, +1 wxp if it's not the first use in the story. All my calculations that suggest it is the best signature involve using it on every roll (ie, 6 times, maybe +-1 once you get a second signature).<br /> Blazing Dragon-Smith Arete costs 15 motes, 1 wp for the project. Also, its power is being brought down by the lowered terminus, but taking advantage of the lower terminus requires spending gxp for the roll, and paying for all your other charms again. Also, it gives +1 wxp for completing the project.<br /> Eternal Omphalos Forge is somewhere in between, costing 15m, 1 wp, 15 gxp for the project, but increasing the terminus needs spending even more to take advantage of it (though you can alternately use it on some very easy project, just to gain a bunch of wp). It also does poorly if you want to work on multiple projects per story, costing +5wxp for the reset<br /> Ephemeral Form Composition is purely for efficiency, and doesn't grant power at all<br /> Fortune-from-Flotsam Ingenuity isn't giving you any benefit to artifacts, instead giving speed on major projects.<br /> <br /> On a different topic, what do people think of the dragon blooded defense penalty negators? (threshold warding stance, flickering candle meditation, blade-deflecting palm doesn't negate penalties but is a good response to them) They seem much weaker than solar ones, in a way that leaves dragon blooded vulnerable to deliberately granting them a bunch of penalties (onslaught/wound/poison/whatever isn't environmental because threshold warding stance is very efficient but focused).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T06:03:55-07:00","id":1207231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1206663-db-charm-commentary-part-1?p=1207225#post1207225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a different topic, what do people think of the dragon blooded defense penalty negators? (threshold warding stance, flickering candle meditation, blade-deflecting palm doesn't negate penalties but is a good response to them) They seem much weaker than solar ones, in a way that leaves dragon blooded vulnerable to deliberately granting them a bunch of penalties (onslaught/wound/poison/whatever isn't environmental because threshold warding stance is very efficient but focused).</div> </div> </div> </div>They should be sufficient for a reasonably well-built character. Poison penalty doesn't apply to Defense, the independent wound penalty negator in Integrity is <i>incredibly </i>effective (for a cohesive group of PCs - if you're playing a bunch of backstabbing assholes who can't afford to have a reasonably strong Intimacy of Loyalty to their teammates, your mileage will vary), so that leaves us with onslaught, which usually isn't too much of an issue (1-2 points can easily be cancelled out by Dodge's penalty negator at a very good price). Multiattack Charms pose something of a problem, but the easy access to Hardness-granting artifact armor shuts down that tactic unless you eat a backloaded IWA (but if you're facing a Solar with that level of Melee investment, at least one person is probably going to have a very bad day on your team no matter what).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T14:03:16-07:00","id":1207407,"title":"","content":"I like it as a flaw personally. Solars get to do the whole thing where they effortlessly shrug off anything that hinders their defence. With DBs it's a bit trickier. The first step to getting past penalties is to not fight in a position where you're on slick smooth rocks during a thunderstorm. If you have to fight in those conditions one or two of you might have a decent negator, but other than that just use tactics to put even more penalties on your foes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T14:42:28-07:00","id":1207415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1206663-db-charm-commentary-part-1?p=1206966#post1206966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't want to talk to people defending the Charm... OK. But I think for the sake of good discussion, you should at least explain your claim to those of us confused by it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, no problem.<br /> <br /> Shadow-Immolating Talon is a charm where you hurt someone for information. It instantly forces an honest confession out of someone to whom you deal health levels of deal damage, e<i>ven if you kill them in the process.</i> It even <i>refunds the cost and doesn't need to be reset</i> when your target doesn't know the answer. You can immediately try it again on your next target.<br /> <br /> Torture in the real world provides the torturer only with whatever the victim thinks the torturer wants to hear. Shadow-Immolating Talon gets you the truth or the fact that your victim doesn't know. This isn't just fantasy-world torture, it's <i>a description of the fantasy that torture proponents have about how torture works</i>. Fast, effective, and without any serious risk of false information. That's why it bothers me. It's not the effects of the charm <i>per se</i> that are problematic, it's how close those effects are to real-world misconceptions that ruin lives.<br /> <br /> Like I said, I don't think that whomever wrote this had this intention. I hope they change things before it goes into print.<br /> <br /> Tangential note: With the bonus effects and the refund, there's no reason an Investigation-heavy Dragon-Blooded wouldn't want to use this on every decisive attack they make, just to see if they can get some unexpected information out of their foes. If you yell &quot;Where is the Scarlet Empress?&quot; on every blow, your enemy either knows and tells you (OMGWTF hooray!), or doesn't know, and you got some bonus dice and double 10s on damage for free.<br /> <br /> Edited to add: also this is not really what I came here to talk about in the first place...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Current project: <a href=\"https://monsterambulance.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Monster Ambulance</a>, wherein you save monsters. In your ambulance.","edited":{"userid":2240,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2240-colin_fredericks","user":"Colin_Fredericks","date":". 04-15-2018, 06:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2240-colin_fredericks","name":"Colin_Fredericks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2240_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T15:41:15-07:00","id":1207423,"title":"","content":"See, that's just hilarious. I'd take the charm just so I could do that.<br /> <br /> Although re-reading the charm that wouldn't work. You get refunded if the target doesn't know, but you also get no extra damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 04-15-2018, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T15:52:05-07:00","id":1207428,"title":"","content":"I agree with you about the fantasy that toruture works (for any purpose other than forcing a confession regardless of accuracy) needs to be rejected, but dealing damage in combat is such an inherently different contextual animal from torture, that Shadow-Immolation Talon is clearly working on different magical principles rather than magically enhancing torture.<br /> <br /> Would you be cool with it if it came with the caveat that it ONLY worked in combat and automatically fails against a restrained captive?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T16:02:51-07:00","id":1207430,"title":"","content":"I still think that this charm reinforces the idea that torture works in the same way that Mountain Crossing Leap Technique reinforces the idea that people can jump over mountains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T16:10:59-07:00","id":1207435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1206663-db-charm-commentary-part-1?p=1207430#post1207430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still think that this charm reinforces the idea that torture works in the same way that Mountain Crossing Leap Technique reinforces the idea that people can jump over mountains.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Kind of a false comparison, because the general public hasn't actually been convinced by media that people can jump over mountains, so that isn't a concern that needs to be considered.<br /> <br /> A charm that let you determine someone's sexual history through a medical examination would carry the same theoretical problem.<br /> <br /> <br /> (I'm not opposed to the Shadow-Immolation Talons, I'm just saying the critique has merit)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T16:23:45-07:00","id":1207438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colin_Fredericks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1206663-db-charm-commentary-part-1?p=1207415#post1207415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Torture in the real world provides the torturer only with whatever the victim thinks the torturer wants to hear. Shadow-Immolating Talon gets you the truth or the fact that your victim doesn't know. This isn't just fantasy-world torture, it's <i>a description of the fantasy that torture proponents have about how torture works</i>. Fast, effective, and without any serious risk of false information. That's why it bothers me. It's not the effects of the charm <i>per se</i> that are problematic, it's how close those effects are to real-world misconceptions that ruin lives.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just think this is a ship that's already sailed. If &quot;torture doesn't work&quot; isn't part of an RPG's core rules it's going to be effective because players can see the outcome of their dice rolls to do things like persuade people and figure out of they're lying. I guess the GM could ignore the dice rolls and have the information be false anyway but that's betraying the player's trust to make a statement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T16:24:31-07:00","id":1207439,"title":"","content":"Shadow-Immolating Talon strikes me as more akin to the Lasso of Truth by way of a Chinese magistrate epic than Jack Bauer. The image I get is of mysticism of flame casting the light of truth where the shadows of deception cannot hide, rather than a person answering a question out of distress from pain.<br /> <br /> \u200bI get not wanting a thread to be wholly about such a subject, but stating that the writers and developers are reinforcing a harmful narrative concerning torture is a serious charge to level.<br /> <br /> \u200bI also think that Dragon Blooded very deliberately did not get a Charm to grapple massive creatures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T16:28:31-07:00","id":1207440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1206663-db-charm-commentary-part-1?p=1207439#post1207439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shadow-Immolating Talon strikes me as more akin to the Lasso of Truth by way of a Chinese magistrate epic than Jack Bauer. The image I get is of mysticism of flame casting the light of truth where the shadows of deception cannot hide, rather than a person answering a question out of distress from pain.<br /> <br /> \u200bI get not wanting a thread to be wholly about such a subject, but stating that the writers and developers are reinforcing a harmful narrative concerning torture is a serious charge to level.<br /> <br /> \u200bI also think that Dragon Blooded very deliberately did not get a Charm to grapple massive creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see where you are coming from, but at the same time I can sympathize with Colin\u2019s position, particularly because fire/pain has very specific connotations when related for information extraction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T17:49:09-07:00","id":1207461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colin_Fredericks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1206663-db-charm-commentary-part-1?p=1207415#post1207415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shadow-Immolating Talon is a charm where you hurt someone for information. It instantly forces an honest confession out of someone to whom you deal health levels of deal damage, e<i>ven if you kill them in the process.</i> It even <i>refunds the cost and doesn't need to be reset</i> when your target doesn't know the answer. You can immediately try it again on your next target.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have access to the text.<br /> <br /> So first off I have an objection to your reading of it. The Charm triggers on a successful attack roll that has to beat Defense and Resolve. The wording is actually a bit unclear if you effectively need to beat both combined or separately. It says, &quot;If the Dragon-Blood\u2019s successes on her attack roll exceeds her target\u2019s Resolve,...&quot; which I would assume means successes after Defense subtracts from your rolled successes, but I can see an argument for rolled successes being need to compared to both independently. Regardless of how hard it really is to pull off though, it doesn't matter if you actually deal damage or not, just that you land a hit with enough successes. As far as I can tell, you can use Gambits as well, so you could Disarm or Grapple someone instead of dealing damage (making the Lasso of Truth image very valid).<br /> <br /> So, yes, a character that wants to torture people could use this Charm to make themselves &quot;better&quot; at it, but it can be used by people that aren't really into torture too.<br /> <br /> Your critique also doesn't separate physical violence influencing social interactions as a whole from torture. Most people would not define, &quot;I demanded the truth and punched them once, then they told me the truth,&quot; as torture. Certainly morally questionable, but in most people's minds torture is more systematic; and doesn't even require physical violence. So there's still a lack of unpacking on this unless &quot;any use of violence to obtain information in any way,&quot; is torture, but that's a hard definition to function with. Which creates a problem with this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Torture in the real world provides the torturer only with whatever the victim thinks the torturer wants to hear. </div> </div> </div>This comes from studies of interrogation techniques (which I agree is a valid and important finding that people need to understand), which can last hours, or days, or weeks, or years. Nobody in the real world thinks you can walk in and slap someone and suddenly they'll tell you everything you want to know. People believe that a confession signed after six hours of psychological tricks played on a suspect that's been held without contact with a lawyer or anyone but police has validity; which is something that needs to be pushed back against. People think that you can waterboard someone three times a day, for a week, and they will tell you something useful; which is something that needs to be pushed back against.<br /> <br /> There's such a big disconnect between &quot;I attack once and inflict a mind control effect on someone,&quot; and &quot;systemic psychological manipulation,&quot; that you're not really addressing here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Shadow-Immolating Talon gets you the truth or the fact that your victim doesn't know. </div> </div> </div>It tells the player that. I don't see where the text says the character knows that. If the Charm doesn't result in an answer to the question, the player might know the difference between not beating their Resolve, and the character simply not knowing, but how does the character actually know more than the Charm didn't work? The player might know the difference between it working properly, and a Defining Intimacy allowing the target to manipulate the answer, but the character doesn't know that. You seem to be translating the assumed mechanical transparency of Exalted with in-character knowledge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fast, effective, and without any serious risk of false information. </div> </div> </div>But there is a risk of false information. If your roll beats their Defense but not their Resolve, the Charm is spent but the target can answer however they want. If the target has a Defining Intimacy they can give you false information. This claim seems to ignore a fairly major set of conditions in the Charm text. A character having higher Resolve than Defense is a serious risk (especially in combat where they might be dealing with Onslaught penalties to their Defense but not Resolve), and lots of Defining Intimacies are a serious risk of getting in the way. Trying the &quot;where is the Scarlet Empress&quot; trick on someone that has a Defining Intimacy towards protecting the Realm's secrets whether they know about where she is or not can let them purposefully mislead your character and send them into all sorts of trouble that your character thinks is true because they trust the Charm.<br /> <br /> If something is so important that a character is tempted to use this Charm on random people, it seems strange that anyone that might know something wouldn't having a relevant Defining Intimacy to throw in the works.<br /> <br /> Running around punching a few thousand people to learn absolutely nothing undermines the idea that this Charm supports the idea that &quot;fantasy torture always works,&quot; since... all you've found out is that a major mystery is a mystery because people don't know what the answers are. And you have a few thousand people now pissed at you for punching them (or the far worse backlash if you've been stabbing people over this). Your character is going to have a lot of social problems if that's what they decide to do when they get this Charm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like I said, I don't think that whomever wrote this had this intention. I hope they change things before it goes into print. </div> </div> </div>What, precisely, would you like to see changed in the Charm? It's a lot easier to get behind advocating this as a group - and thus more likely to succeed - if there's a positive ask rather than just, &quot;fix this to my personal standards.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...or doesn't know, and you got some bonus dice and double 10s on damage for free. </div> </div> </div>This again, seems to be a mistake in reading the rules. The character has to ask the question first, and if the target can't answer, the power goes off - so it 'works' but instantly refunds so there's no effect at all, including the bonuses to the attack. &quot;If a character doesn\u2019t know enough to give the Dragon-Blood an answer, the attack gains no benefits and the cost of this Charm is refunded.&quot; So, basically, the Charm protects you from wasting it on people that can't answer (since the player can't know that ahead of time).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Edited to add: also this is not really what I came here to talk about in the first place... </div> </div> </div>As noted, this is a pretty serious thing. That's why you care about it. Torture is a horrible thing, and we want the game to be responsible in how it handles it, so a claim of handling it irresponsibly is going to be a focal point even with other things said.<br /> <br /> As well there's some community context as well. During the 3e Kickstater with the previews for the different Exalted types, there was a lot of acrimony generated over a certain Abyssal Charm. Even after the developers acknowledge the wording was communicating their intent poorly and tried to clarify it, the game (which wasn't even close to out yet) had forum arguments constantly go into &quot;the devs included a rape ghost Charm!&quot; I at least perceive a desire to avoid repeating that; hence a lot fo the push back in this thread and my desire for a more thorough examination of your stance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 04-15-2018, 08:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T20:26:01-07:00","id":1207515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1206663-db-charm-commentary-part-1?p=1207439#post1207439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shadow-Immolating Talon strikes me as more akin to the Lasso of Truth by way of a Chinese magistrate epic than Jack Bauer. The image I get is of mysticism of flame casting the light of truth where the shadows of deception cannot hide, rather than a person answering a question out of distress from pain.</div> </div> </div> </div>In terms of extracting confessions through force, Shadow-Immolating Talon is a good bit more restrained than Chinese magistrates.<br /> <br /> The Realm is actually a whole lot nicer than it could be, given real-world inspirations.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21733-ascension","name":"Ascension","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21733_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T00:14:04-07:00","id":1207566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1206663-db-charm-commentary-part-1?p=1207439#post1207439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shadow-Immolating Talon strikes me as more akin to the Lasso of Truth by way of a Chinese magistrate epic than Jack Bauer. The image I get is of mysticism of flame casting the light of truth where the shadows of deception cannot hide, rather than a person answering a question out of distress from pain.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly, given Charms like the Fire signature in Bureaucracy, I mostly read it like &quot;the Dragon-Blooded inflames the passions of her target, who can not resist talking about this crime he suddenly feels very strongly about&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T05:31:45-07:00","id":1207620,"title":"","content":"Honestly, that one Investigation charm? Didn't see it as having anything to do with torture, still not seeing it now.<br /> It's got a lot more to do with the classic kind of scene when a character who was wronged by their opponent, generally the protagonist, not only finally gets to defeat them in singular battle, but also get, at last, the truth from them. &quot;Yes! Yes, of course it was I who killed your father, the fool should have known better than to defy me!&quot; &quot;The Heavenly Annihilator? It was hidden in the shrine all along, but I really don't think you'll reach it in time.&quot; &quot;No, of course your birth mother didn't die, you just couldn't find her because it was me all along.&quot;<br /> You know, stuff like that.<br /> Interpreted a certain way... well, sure, you could technically manage to magically torture people to get the truth out of them, but you'll have to choose the victims well, and you're not going to get useful information if they struggle sufficiently against you.<br /> Like, technically, you could use sorcery to enact a genocide as long as the process succeeds, or hurt directly and exclusively very nice and innocent people who just happen to be Creatures of Darkness and so the Sun himself, who is the closest thing to an ultimate moral authority you get, will approve your murder just because that folk was born or made the wrong type of being, or...<br /> Right now I have better things to do than reread core charms to see which ones can be abused in ethically horrifying ways, though, so I trust you folks to find more or declare I got it all wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T07:35:54-07:00","id":1207653,"title":"","content":"All of you make me fantastically happy that I can start a new thread to describe the second half of the charms this week and not need to come back to this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Current project: <a href=\"https://monsterambulance.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Monster Ambulance</a>, wherein you save monsters. In your ambulance.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2240-colin_fredericks","name":"Colin_Fredericks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2240_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T08:43:37-07:00","id":1207666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1207624#post1207624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it be inadvisable to write upgrade Charms that allow Currents Sweep out to Sea and Smashing Tidal Wave Technique to be used with sand and an Earth Aura?<br /> <br /> I\u2019d like Dragon-Blooded to get their Sabaku no Gaara on, but I don\u2019t know if this would break whatever balance you intended Terrestrial Brawl to have between Water and Earth.<br /> <br /> If it doesn\u2019t break anything, then similar upgrades for using those Charms with plants would be great for Wood, though it might need set-up like Arbor Sentinel.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, does that Archery Charm work with any bow, or just those made of wood?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1207648#post1207648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd write separate Earth Brawl Charms that do stuff with sand instead.<br /> <br /> <br /> It works with artifact bows. Flame pieces, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>The implication seems to be that sand-grappling Terrestrial Brawl Charms (and perhaps also vine-grappling Charms) are fully possible, but they would need to be their own things for proper balance.<br /> <br /> This got me to thinking about an artifact gourd of sand.<br /> <br /> It also got me to thinking about an artifact water pouch, for staying hydrated and also ready to use Currents Sweep out to Sea without needing a Water Aura.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T15:33:25-07:00","id":1207779,"title":"","content":"People would have long since stopped using torture as a means to acquire information if it didn't work somewhat. The trouble is that you need to both break the will of the victim and do so in such a way that they know the only way to make the hurting stop is to tell the truth. On top of that, the torturer doesn't know whether if the torture has successfully extracted a piece of truth or if the victim has merely put together some plausible lie to try and make the pain end. Thus any information obtained under duress has to be collated with bits of verifiable information from other sources to see if the information fits with reality, potentially bits wrung from other torture victims This, of course, is complicated by all the other problems of questioning people, such as contaminating witnesses with outside information, determining if you have someone with information in the first place, etc.<br /> <br /> When it comes to Exalted, torture is part of the genre conventions. It's barbaric and savage. It's a staple of despotic overlords to have dungeons where they keep prisoners who they want to see suffer or who might still have useful information that must be extracted at the point of a hot iron. I would not be surprised if some Exalts have turned their talents towards such work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T17:42:13-07:00","id":1207813,"title":"","content":"Is anyone else worried by Inviolate Dragon Spirit? It's already hard to create a decision point. And having someone just shrug it off for 2wp and a mote seems really discouraging.<br /> <br /> Edit: I was just reminded that you can erode intervening intimacies before persuading to bypass the charm. So it's not as strong as I thought. I'll keep the post up for the sake of discussion","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12778,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12778-rustedair","user":"RustedAir","date":". 04-16-2018, 09:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12778-rustedair","name":"RustedAir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12778_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T20:34:42-07:00","id":1207859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colin_Fredericks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1206663-db-charm-commentary-part-1?p=1207653#post1207653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of you make me fantastically happy that I can start a new thread to describe the second half of the charms this week and not need to come back to this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, seriously, chill a bit. We're talking about a game, not the real world. I think these things matter, but you're not helping by throwing shade at everyone that doesn't immediately agree with you.<br /> <br /> If you think a new thread is going to go differently if you decide a Charm there is bad in a similar way and just open up with, &quot;Charm X is pro-[horrible thing].&quot; without any real thorough unpacking of why... you're going to get the same results in the new one.<br /> <br /> If you react to anyone that disagrees with you, or can point out a factually incorrect thing you say, with this kinda thing... again... a new thread isn't going to fix things for you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1206663-db-charm-commentary-part-1?p=1207779#post1207779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People would have long since stopped using torture as a means to acquire information if it didn't work somewhat.</div> </div> </div> </div>People aren't that rational. We do plenty of things that don't work but are how we've always done them anyway.<br /> <br /> Also, a lot of torture is done because the truth isn't what matters, but getting the target to say something the torturer wants the subject to say because it's advantageous to them. This is nothing new, but it still persists because there are incentives.<br /> <br /> It's why I referenced US police interrogation techniques for getting people to sign confessions. Objectively, those results are crap, because the police have become experts in getting people to sign things regardless of the truth. But those confessions are powerful in court, and get convictions (no matter how frequently overturned), clear cases, and so the cops look good on their performance reviews.<br /> <br /> If your incentive is to lay blame on someone convenient rather than the true perpetrator, torture is really tempting. You can get people to confess to what you need a scapegoat for by convincing them it's better than continuing what you're doing to them.<br /> <br /> But actually getting the truth out of a victim? No matter what steps you take, every study shows it doesn't work with nearly enough reliability to trust. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When it comes to Exalted, torture is part of the genre conventions. It's barbaric and savage. It's a staple of despotic overlords to have dungeons where they keep prisoners who they want to see suffer or who might still have useful information that must be extracted at the point of a hot iron. I would not be surprised if some Exalts have turned their talents towards such work. </div> </div> </div>I agree... but I don't think that's Colin's objection to the Charm. The objection (which I don't find compelling at this point) is that the Charm makes torture work even when it shouldn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RustedAir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1206663-db-charm-commentary-part-1?p=1207813#post1207813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is anyone else worried by Inviolate Dragon Spirit? It's already hard to create a decision point. And having someone just shrug it off for 2wp and a mote seems really discouraging.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really worried.<br /> <br /> I mean, &quot;creating a decision point,&quot; just means, &quot;succeeding in a Persuade or Threaten action that the target wants to resist instead of accepting the base outcome.&quot; The Charm doesn't make you immune to retries and all that... so it really just gives you a few more Decision Points to resist social influence while tearing through your WP faster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T22:36:00-07:00","id":1207897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1206663-db-charm-commentary-part-1?p=1207859#post1207859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, a lot of torture is done because the truth isn't what matters, but getting the target to say something the torturer wants the subject to say because it's advantageous to them. This is nothing new, but it still persists because there are incentives.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are mixing torture as a punishment and torture as a means of creating a political fiction with torture as an attempt at extracting information in your answer. The first two aren't really in dispute - those things were done and are done.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But actually getting the truth out of a victim? No matter what steps you take, every study shows it doesn't work with nearly enough reliability to trust. </div> </div> </div>It's not exactly an easy topic to study. Ethics guidelines and classified information are dual barriers on the subject. I generally agree with you - I listed a whole bunch of known caveats to any method of torture. The trouble for us is that torture manages to occasionally yield information - it's why spies taking suicide pills isn't just a thing made up for the movies but has been documented as actual protocol. Torture takes an enemy asset that has failed to respond to lesser coercions - from a Machiavellian perspective a resource otherwise nothing more than a drain on your resources - and turns that asset into a potential information source and also lessens that asset's ability to escape lessened. It's a bit of amoral calculus that will always have an attraction, no matter the problems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I agree... but I don't think that's Colin's objection to the Charm. The objection (which I don't find compelling at this point) is that the Charm makes torture work even when it shouldn't. </div> </div> </div>Isn't that the definition of a Charm? Applying magic to make the impossible possible? We already have Intimidate as an option, something you can perform repeatedly on a restrained captive, so rules for torture effectively exist already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T23:03:30-07:00","id":1207900,"title":"","content":"I meant shouldn't in a meta-sense of &quot;the game shouldn't have it work this way,&quot; rather than shouldn't in the terms of, &quot;Charms shouldn't be allowed to do things that you couldn't accomplish with normal skills.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T05:13:00-07:00","id":1207946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1206663-db-charm-commentary-part-1?p=1207779#post1207779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People would have long since stopped using torture as a means to acquire information if it didn't work somewhat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Torture is effective at getting a prisoner to say what you want them to say. This creates the illusion that it works since it often verifies what the torturer believes to be true.<br /> <br /> If humans stopped using bullshit means to gather information just because the results didn't actually have any relation to reality, &quot;virginity exams&quot; wouldn't have remained a thing for thousands of years till present day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T09:33:24-07:00","id":1208019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1206663-db-charm-commentary-part-1?p=1207946#post1207946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Torture is effective at getting a prisoner to say what you want them to say. This creates the illusion that it works since it often verifies what the torturer believes to be true.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is one of the problems facing anyone using torture, yes. I believe I acknowledged it above. The thing is that it can manage to extract useful information, especially if you are dealing with things that are difficult to search for but easy to verify, such as a physical location or the cipher key for a coded message. This is what makes torture a constant moral conundrum. In wartime, information can save the lives of your people. Do you stain your hands with torture or do you forever wonder how much blood is on your hands because you didn't?<br /> <br /> I don't support the use of torture. It's too easy to make it your hammer in a world of nails. But support the claim that torture doesn't ever work? That's factually inaccurate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If humans stopped using bullshit means to gather information just because the results didn't actually have any relation to reality, &quot;virginity exams&quot; wouldn't have remained a thing for thousands of years till present day. </div> </div> </div>From my understanding of what constitutes a &quot;virginity exam&quot;, that's just the closest thing to physical evidence you can get. Yes, it has a high rate of both false positives and false negatives, but you seem to be faulting people for trying to put a scientific standard to a problem. I suspect your real problem is with the reasons why they want to know rather than the how.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T13:57:29-07:00","id":1208161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1206663-db-charm-commentary-part-1?p=1208019#post1208019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...but you seem to be faulting people for trying to put a scientific standard to a problem. I suspect your real problem is with the reasons why they want to know rather than the how.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both are valid criticisms.<br /> <br /> Science has limits on what it can analyze. Science can't address a hypothesis that isn't falsifiable. Trying to use the scientific standard on a problem that lacks falsifiable status is something we can fault people for; they're using the wrong tool for the problem. There is no biological state of &quot;virginity.&quot; Any test of virginity is scientifically invalid because there's no way to empirically observe virginity, as it isn't something that exists in material form.<br /> <br /> And of course, there's plenty of reason to have issue with the cultural norms that reinforce virginity tests because it's very unhealthy form of social behavioral control. Though there's a third issue of the having a real problem with not why it is being done, or the precise procedure in question, but how they're done in a performative sense. That is, virginity exams aren't some private procedure done between a person and their doctor with all the protections of confidentiality done solely for the mental well being of the person requesting it be done. They're public performances where a person's physical body and privacy is being tossed aside to assuage public interests in what isn't a public matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T00:42:16-07:00","id":1208353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1206663-db-charm-commentary-part-1?p=1208161#post1208161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Science has limits on what it can analyze. Science can't address a hypothesis that isn't falsifiable. Trying to use the scientific standard on a problem that lacks falsifiable status is something we can fault people for; they're using the wrong tool for the problem. There is no biological state of &quot;virginity.&quot; Any test of virginity is scientifically invalid because there's no way to empirically observe virginity, as it isn't something that exists in material form.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Has had sex at least once&quot; is a reasonably falsifiable claim.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And of course, there's plenty of reason to have issue with the cultural norms that reinforce virginity tests because it's very unhealthy form of social behavioral control. Though there's a third issue of the having a real problem with not why it is being done, or the precise procedure in question, but how they're done in a performative sense. That is, virginity exams aren't some private procedure done between a person and their doctor with all the protections of confidentiality done solely for the mental well being of the person requesting it be done. They're public performances where a person's physical body and privacy is being tossed aside to assuage public interests in what isn't a public matter. </div> </div> </div>Mostly agreed. Any real practical concerns died back in the Iron Age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T01:39:38-07:00","id":1208358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1206663-db-charm-commentary-part-1?p=1208353#post1208353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Has had sex at least once&quot; is a reasonably falsifiable claim.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. And, of course, there's no functional test for it besides direct observation. The prevailing issue is that &quot;virginity&quot; is a loose social construct with multiple definitions around the concept of a lack of sexual experience. What counts as an act that results in the loss of virginity is in a constant state of cultural flux. There's no universal acceptance of which sex acts remove virginity and which don't. For example, heterosexual couples frequently use a much stricter definition of penetrative vaginal intercourse so they can remain virgins despite doing other things, while LGBTQ+ individuals frequently express a much looser concept of virginity if they even hold to it at all since vagina penetration might not be possible at all in a given relationship, and this is a current issue in scientific study of sexual behavioral patterns because the 'traditional' definition is one now recognized to have a significant heterosexual bias that's not useful for getting a solid idea of average rates of sexual activity within a population/demographic. There are unsettled (because there is no actual settling of them) debates on whether climax is necessary, consent is necessary (which is an older debate that some people might imagine), bloody discharge is necessary, and if virginity can be maintained or even regained despite having had sex.<br /> <br /> So &quot;virginity&quot; remains beyond science, because it isn't something that can be falsified even if specific claims that are frequently linked to the concept of virginity can be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T06:35:40-07:00","id":1208421,"title":"","content":"So we have the rest of the Dragon-Blooded Charmset now. Do you guys maybe possibly want to talk about those?<br /> <br /> Like, how cool the new Dragon Vortex Technique is?<br /> <br /> Or how nice it is that Lore lets you give motes, an Elemental Aura, and even a level of your anima banner to someone else, all with the same Charm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T18:30:11-07:00","id":1208655,"title":"","content":"Is it just me, or is Observer Awareness Method very hard to avoid? If they can get 1 success on a roll, they always know if they're being observed.<br /> Knowing your location is harder, but my reading of comparing the roll to (stealth) is the sneaker can't use an excellency or stunts or willpower, and plenty of people will want to hide who don't have great guile.<br /> Also, as a reflexive charm costing 1 mote, it's very easy to activate it repeatedly until you get lucky on the check, or the person observing you runs out of motes to boost their guile.<br /> Also, since it doesn't offer a roll by the hider, or rely on any senses, or involve an awareness charm, very few charms interact with it. Maybe the more mental of the solar stealth charms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T04:59:27-07:00","id":1208801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1206663-db-charm-commentary-part-1?p=1208655#post1208655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it just me, or is Observer Awareness Method very hard to avoid? If they can get 1 success on a roll, they always know if they're being observed.<br /> Knowing your location is harder, but my reading of comparing the roll to (stealth) is the sneaker can't use an excellency or stunts or willpower, and plenty of people will want to hide who don't have great guile.<br /> Also, as a reflexive charm costing 1 mote, it's very easy to activate it repeatedly until you get lucky on the check, or the person observing you runs out of motes to boost their guile.<br /> Also, since it doesn't offer a roll by the hider, or rely on any senses, or involve an awareness charm, very few charms interact with it. Maybe the more mental of the solar stealth charms?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dragonblood has to beat the higher of stealth or guile. You can definitely increase your guile through various means, and I have to assume that this is a stealth roll as opposed to just the stealth skill, so that can be likewise increased.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T10:14:04-07:00","id":1209306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1206663-db-charm-commentary-part-1?p=1208421#post1208421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So we have the rest of the Dragon-Blooded Charmset now. Do you guys maybe possibly want to talk about those?<br /> <br /> Like, how cool the new Dragon Vortex Technique is?<br /> <br /> Or how nice it is that Lore lets you give motes, an Elemental Aura, and even a level of your anima banner to someone else, all with the same Charm?</div> </div> </div> </div>I started <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1209253-db-charm-commentary-part-2\">a new thread</a>. And yes, new Dragon Vortex 100% rocks. (Well, if you've got a full circle using it then it 20% rocks and 20% fire and...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Current project: <a href=\"https://monsterambulance.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Monster Ambulance</a>, wherein you save monsters. In your ambulance.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2240-colin_fredericks","name":"Colin_Fredericks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2240_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}